---
import { LinkButton } from "@astrojs/starlight/components";

import Icon from "@components/Icon.astro";
---

<section id="begin-here" class="begin-here">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="content-container">
      <h2>Begin here</h2>
      <p>
        Ready to bring your smart home ideas to life? Grab a board (such as an ESP32 development board) and install in
        the way that suits you:
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card-columns">
      <div class="card-column">
        <div class="card card-bgc">
          <div class="card__content">
            <Icon icon="hardware" class="card__icon" />
            <p class="card__title h2">Choose your hardware</p>
            <p>
              EmbedMe supports a wide range of ESP32, ESP8266, RP2040, and Tuya-based microcontrollers. If you’re new to
              this type of hardware, any inexpensive ESP32 development board is a great place to start – check the
              components documentation for the specific peripherals your project needs.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="card__content">
            <LinkButton href="/components/" class="card__text-link" icon="right-arrow" iconPlacement="start"
              >Browse components</LinkButton
            >
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card-column">
        <div class="card card-bgc">
          <Icon icon="build" class="card__icon" />
          <p class="card__title h2">For the simplest setup: ESPHome Desktop App</p>
          <p>A complete package containing everything you need to install with one click.</p>
          <p>Available for Windows, macOS, and Linux.</p>

          <LinkButton href="/install/" class="card__text-link" icon="right-arrow" iconPlacement="start"
            >Download Desktop App</LinkButton
          >
        </div>

        <div class="card card-bgc">
          <Icon icon="build" class="card__icon" />
          <p class="card__title h2">A step-by-step guide</p>
          <p>
            Our documentation walks you through everything from setting up your first device to more advanced
            configurations. Begin with our Get Started guide, then explore from there.
          </p>

          <LinkButton href="/install/getting-started/" class="card__text-link" icon="right-arrow" iconPlacement="start"
            >Open the Get Started guide</LinkButton
          >
        </div>

        <div class="card card-bgc">
          <Icon icon="extension" class="card__icon" />
          <p class="card__title h2">Ready-Made Projects: The fast route to a finished device</p>
          <p>
            While installing ESPHome gives you freedom to build smart home devices your way, you may not need custom
            configuration. If you just want to quickly turn a board into a Bluetooth proxy, voice assistant, or media
            player for example, our Ready-Made Projects are the answer. They’re pre-configured to work with Home
            Assistant straightaway, so you can install them directly from your browser in a single click: no need to
            install ESPHome.
          </p>

          <LinkButton href="/projects/" class="card__text-link" icon="right-arrow" iconPlacement="start"
            >Explore Ready-Made Projects</LinkButton
          >
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style lang="scss">
  @use "../../styles/mixins" as *;

  .begin-here {
    .content-container {
      @include bp(tablet) {
        max-width: 50%;
      }
    }

    .card-columns {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 1.5rem;
      margin-top: 1.5rem;

      @include bp(desktop) {
        flex-direction: row;
        align-items: flex-start;
        margin-top: 3rem;
      }
    }

    .card-column {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 1.5rem;

      @include bp(desktop) {
        flex: 1 1 50%;
      }

      .card {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;

        @include bp(desktop) {
          flex: 1;
        }
      }

      :global(.card__text-link) {
        margin-top: auto;
        padding-top: 1.25rem;
      }

      &:first-child {
        @include bp(desktop) {
          position: sticky;
          top: calc(var(--sl-nav-height) + 2rem);
        }
      }
    }

    .card {
      &__icon {
        margin-bottom: 1rem;
      }

      &__content {
        @include bp(tablet) {
          flex-basis: 50%;
        }
      }
    }
  }
</style>
